                            <comment id="16583939" author="ivan.glukos" created="Fri, 17 Aug 2018 13:28:23 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;From my point of view, the correct fix is:&lt;br/&gt;
1) PageMemoryImpl#beforeReleaseWrite - save real page ID (can be read via PageIO#getPageId) to PageSnapshot instead of the passed one. We can also assert here that passed effectivePageId is equal to saved inside page.&lt;br/&gt;
2) GridCacheDatabaseSharedManager#restoreMemory - when processing PAGE_RECORD, acquire writeLock with restore = true flag (this will enforce skipping of tag check).&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="16707262" author="ilantukh" created="Mon, 3 Dec 2018 14:19:05 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;I don&apos;t see any problem in PageMemory code, only in PageMemoryTracker (which is just a testing utility).&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
